+# Private native CUDA resource benchmark
+
+This ignored qualification batch is distinct from product management and tiny
+component GpuProbeReservation. It retains one original fixed3600-second native
+batch cutoff plus the maintained original3600-second external parent. Each of
+one load, one warmup and
+twenty predeclared maximum-input samples has its own original120-second cutoff.
+It never increases the120-second
+product request or125-second delivery budget. No retry or denominator change.
+Complete Context17/128/8192 numeric and twelve-case Focus numeric remain separate
+component proofs using their existing single120-second owner.
+
+A native Rust request emitter serializes scalar pins and explicit host/device/
+Job bounds. Request data is not an execution permit. One actual private-control
+ServiceLease, NativeInferenceOwner, Kernel optional host reservation and actual
+native GPU device/session are retained through the whole benchmark. The same
+session and source serve all21 forwards. Current native ResourcePolicy supplies
+8192 shared/Context, Focus512, N8, twenty samples and nearest-rank p95 index18.
+The original actual max-input compiler is reused; no shorter tensor substitute.
+
+The complete forward labels (warmup then samples1 through20), original input
+digest and actual final placement are durably retained before the first score.
+The actual native attention_backend_plan, when present, authenticates its graph,
+operator/dtype/node roster; it is separate from stock per-forward backend debug
+output. A forward is appended to completed only after actual scorer success and
+native sync. One Scorer.score_with_deadline means one actual Session.run.
+No completion is inferred from journal operations, expected labels or logs.
+
+The existing journal gains a bounded per-operation absolute-expiry entry, with
+unchanged historical create/observe behavior and event schema. Each expiry is
+fixed before start fsync, clipped to the original native batch cutoff and never
+renewed after observer IO. Provider Instant is captured conservatively before native QPC
+sampling; the original native journal expiry is the external watchdog authority.
+The maintained owned Resource20 parent remains required for unreturned FFI,
+actual image/SID/Job ownership, commit/RSS/log watches and real settlement.
+
+Host peak comes from actual persistent process RSS and strict original bounds.
+GPU free/total capacity comes only from the existing authenticated native device
+observer. These are occupancy/headroom observations, not process GPU peak.
+measured_peak_device_bytes stays null and final_gpu_qualification stays false:
+ORT1.30 arena stats alone exclude context/library allocations and current pinned
+Rust ORT API22 lacks API23 AllocatorGetStats. Neither reserved bytes nor free-memory
+delta nor a scoped allocator maximum may replace an unavailable process peak.
+A complete latency/placement/host series can pass independently; dependent final
+GPU qualification remains blocked until genuine complete peak evidence exists.
+
+First native error/overrun/host excess stops the remaining population. Core partial
+series remains truthful with no fabricated zero or partial p95. Unknown CUDA work
+retains actual source/session/lease/host claim/native owner/control root. Actual
+scorer teardown precedes release/poison/claim observations; complete input hashes,
+control cleanup and final persistent RSS are retained before final whole cutoff.
+No advice, calibration, scientific-to-product transfer or product Ready follows.
+
+Original explicit host/Job ceilings remain Focus4/8GiB, Compact16/32GiB and
+Large40/48GiB from their retained owned Resource20 cards. A metadata variant
+cannot silently change that pair; other historical models refuse. Actual process
+and Job both retain the Job containment ceiling; separate parent commit watches
+and native persistent RSS remain distinct from that cap.
+
+The metadata-only emitter writes a native policy sidecar with exact model pairs,
+Core ResourcePolicy and literal1/1/20 schedule. The parent consumes that native
+output and authenticates its BenchmarkRequest wrapper, then the nested original
+Core ResourceRunInput unchanged. Native journal identity binds wrapper SHA; model,
+profile and source bind the nested Core owner. The original external parent
+cutoff starts before process creation and remains independently authoritative:
+this later native batch clock cannot extend it or manufacture parent settlement.
+
+The NN0 request emitter also compiles the exact maximum resource input using the
+existing Compiler::from_verified, compiler/tokenizer pins and original source
+fixture. No Scorer or weight load is used. A fresh expectations sidecar records
+that complete CompiledInput, model/profile/Core policy and22 native operation
+slots with real input digests. BenchmarkRequest pins it. The actual benchmark
+reconstructs this metadata expectation before load, then independently compares
+the actual resident Scorer compiler's complete result before the first forward.
+The Python parent reads these native outputs; it never constructs Core input or
+native roster fields. Expected data grants no completion or execution authority.
